  "definition": "Citalopram is a selective serotonin reuptake inhibitor used as an antidepressant. It has also been reported as effective in reducing ethanol intake in people with alcoholism and may be preferred over tricyclic antidepressants in depressed patients with tardive dyskinesia because tricyclics can worsen that movement problem.",
